                <pb facs="0486" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg381"/>


                <head>Note From Leddy to Carson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-11-29">November 29,
                        1958</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d111-3" n="3" type="facsimile" xml:id="d111-3"/>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Basic National Policy
                    Problem</hi></p>
                <p>Mr. Dillon has approved the attached
                    memorandum from Mr. Smith to the Secretary regarding an approach to the
                    President. However, he <pb facs="0487" n="382" type="typeset" xml:id="pg382"/>
                    believes that it would be unwise for the Secretary to mention the Specific
                    example of a national sales tax, which is a controversial form of taxation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">John M. Leddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
